// A DMA-SERVICED transfer, from the controller's side: arm it, then wait.
//
// completes_when: nbytes bytes have been shifted and SPI_STATUS.done is set.
// waits for:      the DMA channel wired to this controller to move every word.
//
// THE BODY IS SHORT BECAUSE THE OTHER HALF IS SOMEBODY ELSE'S. The processor's
// entire job in a DMA-serviced transfer is to arm both ends and wait; the words
// move between the FIFO and memory without it. That asymmetry -- almost no code
// on this side, a whole channel programming sequence on the other -- is the
// thing this model is trying to show, so it gets its own named operation rather
// than being inlined into the two actions that call it.
//
// It requires SPI_CTRL.dma_en to have been configured (spi_c/actions/ constrains
// it). Without it the controller never raises its request line, the DMA channel
// never sees a request, and this waits forever -- a hang, not an error, which is
// exactly why the requirement is a constraint the solver enforces rather than a
// check this function could make.
import spi_types_pkg::*;

extend component spi_c {

    target function void dma_transfer(spi_dir_e dir, bit[32] nbytes) {
        start_transfer(dir, nbytes);
        wait_done();
    }
}
